{"c":[{"id":"48eb9dd5962c5d4c","sum":"W3-B26: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply; MemoryStore grants no authority; push v2/* only to sam; never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; Jev confidence = top-two margin; Groq 8k tok/min, space calls with fresh AbortSignal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ff412afe096d8651","sum":"W3/B25: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply; MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory and grants no authority; oxc needs   escaped. Push v2/* only to sam. Intents gpt-oss-120b, plans qwen3.8 (~1k out tok/min); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c539feeaf5360a4d","sum":"W3: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory (real folder only without --data-dir) and grants no authority (that stays in memory.sqlite). oxc rejects raw U+2028 in a regex; write \\u2028.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3: client setCodeSigningRequirement blocks what it receives, not its first call; XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory is markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory; main.ts uses the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, hand-off stay in memory.sqlite); editing a skill file puts it back on Tab (SkillJson.fileDigest). oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal; write the \\u2028 escape (Write tools may unescape it).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e60e3e751e2435c2","sum":"Remotes and Groq writers: push v2/* only to remote sam; Ask intents use gpt-oss-120b, plan programs qwen3.8 (about 1,000 output tokens a minute and 200k a day); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal after each wait. U+2731 marks required labels on the job form.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2ebd6c0099fdfde","sum":"Push v2/* only to remote sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret); origin is the team hackathon repo. Ask intents use INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8, ~1,000 output tokens/min, 200k/day on Groq); gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T210855Z-22a0908ac8155d26","text":"Push v2/* branches to the remote named sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret), where their PRs live. origin is the team hackathon repo (theodorexli/hackathon-2026-09-19); a bare 'git push origin' publishes there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-2bd567d78f578d5c","text":"B25: Ask intents go to INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs to WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day ran out during dev runs, and gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400 'does not match the expected schema'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b1d476e32a92cb95","sum":"B25: writers that space calls must give each request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait (a 15 s gap aborted every call); the job form marks required labels with U+2731, which realfill normLabel strips.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-3925313f151b5275","text":"B25: eval writers that space calls must give the request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait; a 15 s gap aborted every intent in planner-eval's first GUI run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-9174d67891bff255","text":"B25: the job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it, and B24's scoreboards counted those four fields as not found.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0039d51d111ccafa","sum":"B25-B26/D2-02: never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; bridge sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; Ask sentences in planner/says.ts; Jev 'confidence' is the top-two margin; Groq gpt-oss-120b allows 8k tok/min (space Ask evals 30 s); a one-token Groq probe hides a spent day.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97c4b1112eed6f12","sum":"B25/W4/B26: never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; captcha frames via compose.ts unit tests; bridge sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; a one-token Groq probe hides a spent day.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e7d7ded421a71b5d","sum":"B25/W4: never-typed kinds live only in memory/sensitive.ts (extend it, no second list). HSTS-preloaded captcha hosts can't be pointed at a local server; test captcha frames via extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-bc8230171f42cb4e","text":"B25: never-typed kinds (fill, planner, Ask) are memory/sensitive.ts, M1's classifier copied unchanged from v2/memory; extend that file, never a second list.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220624Z-f865060dd10d04a3","text":"W4: hcaptcha/recaptcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so --host-resolver-rules cannot point a test browser's captcha frame at a local http server (the load hangs); test captcha frame composition through extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c32ace5fe4e098f","sum":"W4/B26: bridge test sockets a fixture accept()s need SO_NOSIGPIPE or signal 13 kills the run. Groq answers a one-token probe after a model's daily tokens run out; only a real-size request shows the 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T223033Z-e64c70b59e406a7f","text":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a test socket that a fixture accept()s needs SO_NOSIGPIPE, or a write after the peer closed kills the whole run with signal 13, blamed on whichever test was running.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-04a43869ad872043","text":"B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even when a model's tokens-per-day is spent; only a real-size request shows the 429 TPD. gpt-oss-120b's day ran out during B26's first Ask run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"B26/D2-02: Ask sentences live in planner/says.ts; generator measurements pin setGeneratorClock; Jev 'confidence' is the top-two margin; Groq gpt-oss-120b allows 8k tokens/min, so Ask evals space calls 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask refusals and questions live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message for the user, detail for ids and provider errors); offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold forms hit the time budget.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the top-two margin (0.75 needs ~0.875 on the winner); Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min, so Ask evals space calls 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b4fb8385e296a602","sum":"D2-02..B29: routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle); fixtures await waitForLoad after navigating; scope words are allowlists, exclusion words end name trust; controls ride FillHandoff; boxes tick only for a question; differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"077248175b9b025f","sum":"D2-02/B27/B28: routed producers hold offers until chosen; Router 1 answers near the 0.5 floor flip between runs; score B17/B18 with b27/memsets relabels; fixtures need waitForLoad after navigation; Ask scope words are scope-words.ts allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bae047d115123a98","sum":"D2-02/B27: no routing = producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers until chosen (await routing.idle, routedSettled). Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of the 0.5 floor flip run to run; diff per moment. Failed fills reach the user only via Helper.fillFailed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3ae20362fc05a5eb","sum":"D2-02/B27: routing absent keeps producers self-triggering; routed producers hold offers until chosen (await routing.idle then routedSettled). B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last 'none'; score with relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02/B27: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of the 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs; diff runs per moment before crediting a code change. A failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9e36f49db21c9173","sum":"B28 web-form fixtures: wait for site.waitForLoad after a navigation before the next site.command; accept.ts can't use executor.run (native watchInput gives noWindow); Ask scope words are scope-words.ts allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or it hits the departing page's long poll and times out. (B28's 'accept.ts cannot run executor.run' was lifted in D2-04.)","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2fcc93ff7d0331d","sum":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: a whole-form or section scope counts only if the whole instruction is a scope-words grammar sentence. Matching labels or searching inside failed open 8 times.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044915Z-bf6a7f62ff27c59b","text":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: only FILLER may stand beside a whole-form or section phrase, and a source phrase must open with a preposition. Matching field labels in the rest failed open three times.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T060231Z-5982020e0a78f148","text":"B28: Ask trusts a whole-form or section scope only if the whole normalized instruction is a scope-words.ts grammar sentence, and a section only under one un-nested heading that is wholly the user's own. Searching inside after stripping sources/titles/quotes failed open 5 times.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"16aeb5fd1a76ee7a","sum":"B28b/D2-04/B29: exclusion words drop name trust; boxes tick only for a question label; controls never ride FillField.value; ledger 'after' is intended, differing read-back = mayIncludeInput; number undo compares numerically; RESTRICTS matches 'without using X'.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c6f40c96b6283efc","sum":"B28b/D2-04: EXCLUSION_WORDS end name trust; SECTION trusts only fields of its meaning. A control's value never rides FillField.value. A box gets a tick only for a question to the user (boxKind). accept.ts runs executor tasks on page windows.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6936d2244b2292af","sum":"B28b: an Ask with an EXCLUSION_WORDS word (scope-words.ts) gets no name trust; a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning. D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value; Fill all writes controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T063813Z-3bd79ae87e6b8e79","text":"B28b: an Ask instruction with a scope-words.ts EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust (Jev confirms every field); a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning (isContactField; up top, my details: none). Restriction word lists stay open; each review found more.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080809Z-f16da6d6064b889b","text":"D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value (zod and the host decoder refuse it on any control but text); a Fill all writes the controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true, through writtenFields.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4fad04d8f129b479","sum":"D2-04: a box gets a tick only when its label is a question to the user (fill/controls.ts boxKind); never widen it by adding consent words. accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept runs executor tasks on page windows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0265fdcfcf17917c","text":"D2-04: a box gets a tick by its label's kind (fill/controls.ts boxKind: only a question to the user may be written, a first-person statement never gets a value); consent word lists failed open in both reviews, so never widen the box rule by adding words alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0557296abbc22e11","text":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept now runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's 'accept cannot run executor.run' no longer holds); page input still comes from the extension's guard.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b8f8d8cc08d8e1b1","sum":"D2-04/B29: radio peers found tree-wide by name+form owner; ledger 'after' is the intended value, a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput (undo refuses); number fields compare numerically for undo only; RESTRICTS matches 'without using X' (tests say 'not from X').","tree":{"c":[{"id":"50990865af94b806","sum":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner (the form attribute). B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the intended value; a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it, as for pre-B29 rows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-c2d09e45a7621952","text":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner: a button outside its form element joins it through the form attribute. The walker's radioPeers and the content script's otherChecked both searched the form element only.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092126Z-f0c295d458383a43","text":"B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the value Caret meant to write; a read-back that differs sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it. Journal rows without afterIntended (saved before B29) recover their confirmed writes as mayIncludeInput.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33a32dbecb06c39a","sum":"B29: page number fields compare as numbers for undo identity only (executor.ts canonicalDecimal, not Number()); sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X' (no source question), so excluded-window tests say 'not from X'.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2a54c50194565255","text":"B29: page number fields (type=number, inputmode numeric/decimal -> PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity only, through executor.ts canonicalDecimal; Number() made 9007199254740993 equal 9007199254740992.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2d5fb1876e453777","text":"B29: sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X', and such an instruction gets no source question; tests of an excluded source window use 'not from X'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
